    "result_text": "The build is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required the owner JSON to expose `initials` as the upper-cased first letters of first/last name, dot-separated with a trailing dot (`J.S.`).\n\nI made two minimal changes:\n\n1. **`Person.java`** \u2014 added a small `getInitials()` method (CC 1). I placed it in `Person` rather than `Owner` because `firstName`/`lastName` live there and `Person`'s surrounding complexity (`WMC_other`) is just four trivial getters/setters, versus `Owner`'s large method set. MapStruct auto-maps the `getInitials()` getter onto the DTO's `initials` field by name, so no mapper edit was needed.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `initials` property (readOnly string) to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field for serialization.\n\nBecause MapStruct picks up the getter automatically, I avoided touching `OwnerMapper` or any function \u2014 keeping structural impact to one tiny new method plus a schema entry across two files. Both the new `AcceptanceTest` and the full suite pass.",
